,{"href":93,"rel":94},"https:\u002F\u002Fgithub.com\u002Fmarcus-universe\u002FSoundNinja\u002Fblob\u002Fmain\u002FLICENSE",[32],"GPL-3.0",[18,97,99],{"id":98},"mentions-légales","Mentions légales",[14,101,102,103,77],{},"Mentions légales et coordonnées : ",[28,104,99],{"href":105},"\u002Fimpressum",{"title":107,"searchDepth":108,"depth":108,"links":109},"",2,[110,111,112,113,114],{"id":20,"depth":108,"text":21},{"id":48,"depth":108,"text":49},{"id":59,"depth":108,"text":60},{"id":80,"depth":108,"text":81},{"id":98,"depth":108,"text":99},"Où obtenir de l’aide et signaler des bugs.","md",{},true,8,"\u002Fsupport",{"title":5,"description":115},"4CL2vdjAjeBD6Jr7vz0bxGWlJWlax0WoUFYh-B-Seqk",[124,253,468,616,1019,1155,1302,1523],{"id":125,"title":126,"body":127,"description":246,"extension":116,"meta":247,"navigation":118,"order":248,"path":249,"seo":250,"stem":251,"__hash__":252},"content_fr\u002Foverview.md","Aperçu",{"type":7,"value":128,"toc":240},[129,132,135,138,141,145,161,165,204,208,215,219],[10,130,126],{"id":131},"aperçu",[14,133,134],{},"SoundNinja est un soundboard open source pour le live streaming, les discussions entre amis et l’enregistrement de podcasts. Il est construit avec Tauri v2 et Nuxt 4 pour rester léger en RAM et sur le disque.",[14,136,137],{},"Le but est simple : garder une énorme bibliothèque de sons facile à parcourir, puis jouer le bon clip en quelques millisecondes. L’interface marche aussi comme tableau de bord en VR.",[14,139,140],{},"SoundNinja est encore en développement précoce. Les fonctions marchent, mais toutes les plateformes ne sont pas entièrement testées.",[18,142,144],{"id":143},"pour-qui","Pour qui",[146,147,148,152,155,158],"ul",{},[149,150,151],"li",{},"Les streameurs qui ont besoin de cues sonores instantanés",[149,153,154],{},"Les amis qui veulent un board partagé pour le vocal",[149,156,157],{},"Les podcasteurs qui enregistrent des clips et les posent sur un board",[149,159,160],{},"Quiconque veut un soundboard personnalisable et local-first",[18,162,164],{"id":163},"ce-que-tu-peux-faire","Ce que tu peux faire",[146,166,167,170,173,176,179,182,185,188,191,198,201],{},[149,168,169],{},"Construire un soundboard à partir de tes propres fichiers audio",[149,171,172],{},"Organiser les sons dans des onglets colorés, des groupes, des tags et la recherche",[149,174,175],{},"Filtrer par tags (OU) et trier par nom, date, durée ou taille",[149,177,178],{},"Sélection multiple avec rectangle ou plage Maj, puis couleur, déplacement ou suppression en lot",[149,180,181],{},"Régler le volume par son depuis le menu contextuel",[149,183,184],{},"Concevoir le look avec le Theme Creator",[149,186,187],{},"Enregistrer l’audio du PC ou un micro dans le Record Editor",[149,189,190],{},"Assigner des raccourcis à des sons individuels",[149,192,193,194],{},"Déclencher des sons depuis ",[28,195,197],{"href":196},"\u002Fdocs\u002Fremote-control","Bitfocus Companion",[149,199,200],{},"Importer et exporter un soundboard complet pour le partager",[149,202,203],{},"Utiliser des GIF ou des images sur les boutons — bibliothèque de dossiers locale ou KLIPY",[18,205,207],{"id":206},"licence","Licence",[14,209,210,211,214],{},"SoundNinja est un logiciel libre sous ",[28,212,95],{"href":93,"rel":213},[32],". Forke-le, modifie-le, partage-le.",[18,216,218],{"id":217},"prochaines-étapes","Prochaines étapes",[220,221,222,228,234],"ol",{},[149,223,224],{},[28,225,227],{"href":226},"\u002Fdocs\u002Finstallation","Installer SoundNinja",[149,229,230],{},[28,231,233],{"href":232},"\u002Fdocs\u002Fadding-sounds","Ajouter des sons",[149,235,236],{},[28,237,239],{"href":238},"\u002Fdocs\u002Forganizing-sounds","Organiser ton board",{"title":107,"searchDepth":108,"depth":108,"links":241},[242,243,244,245],{"id":143,"depth":108,"text":144},{"id":163,"depth":108,"text":164},{"id":206,"depth":108,"text":207},{"id":217,"depth":108,"text":218},"Ce qu’est SoundNinja et ce que tu peux en faire.",{},1,"\u002Foverview",{"title":126,"description":246},"overview","nBakDXsUbMnm0zyn8m6jAooziqocGWiZV3EwAtrg0xk",{"id":254,"title":255,"body":256,"description":463,"extension":116,"meta":464,"navigation":118,"order":108,"path":465,"seo":466,"stem":260,"__hash__":467},"content_fr\u002Finstallation.md","Installation",{"type":7,"value":257,"toc":456},[258,261,272,276,296,299,303,317,320,324,349,360,362,368,372,386,416,431,452],[10,259,255],{"id":260},"installation",[14,262,263,264,266,267,271],{},"Récupère un build sur la ",[28,265,70],{"href":69}," ou sur ",[28,268,76],{"href":269,"rel":270},"https:\u002F\u002Fgithub.com\u002Fmarcus-universe\u002FSoundNinja\u002Freleases\u002Flatest",[32],". SoundNinja est en développement précoce — traite les builds comme des bêtas.",[18,273,275],{"id":274},"windows","Windows",[146,277,278,287,290,293],{},[149,279,280,41,283,286],{},[38,281,282],{},"Installateur (.exe)",[38,284,285],{},"MSI (.msi)"," pour Windows 64 bits",[149,288,289],{},"Cible de la landing page : Windows 10 et plus",[149,291,292],{},"Le README de l’app mentionne aussi Windows 8 et supérieur",[149,294,295],{},"L’installateur NSIS est sombre. Choisis une langue à l’installation — SoundNinja la retient au prochain lancement.",[14,297,298],{},"Lance l’installateur, puis ouvre SoundNinja depuis le menu Démarrer.",[18,300,302],{"id":301},"macos","macOS",[146,304,305,311,314],{},[149,306,307,310],{},[38,308,309],{},".dmg universel"," pour Apple Silicon et Intel",[149,312,313],{},"Cible de la landing page : macOS 10.14 et plus",[149,315,316],{},"Le README de l’app mentionne macOS 10.15 et supérieur",[14,318,319],{},"Ouvre l’image disque et glisse SoundNinja dans Applications.",[18,321,323],{"id":322},"linux","Linux",[146,325,326,332,338,346],{},[149,327,328,331],{},[38,329,330],{},"Debian (.deb)"," pour Ubuntu \u002F Debian",[149,333,334,337],{},[38,335,336],{},"AppImage"," pour les autres distros",[149,339,340,341,345],{},"Après publication d’une release, les utilisateurs Arch peuvent installer ",[342,343,344],"code",{},"soundninja-bin"," depuis l’AUR",[149,347,348],{},"Testé sur Ubuntu 20.04",[14,350,351,352,355,356,359],{},"Les builds desktop ont besoin des paquets WebKit et GTK. Sous Debian\u002FUbuntu, ça veut souvent dire ",[342,353,354],{},"libwebkit2gtk",", ",[342,357,358],{},"libgtk-3-0"," et une bibliothèque app-indicator.",[18,361,60],{"id":59},[14,363,364,365,367],{},"Dans l’app, ouvre ",[38,366,40],{},". Tu peux aussi laisser SoundNinja vérifier au démarrage dans les Paramètres.",[18,369,371],{"id":370},"compiler-depuis-les-sources","Compiler depuis les sources",[14,373,374,375,379,380,385],{},"Besoin d’un build custom ? Clone ",[28,376,378],{"href":87,"rel":377},[32],"le repo",", installe les ",[28,381,384],{"href":382,"rel":383},"https:\u002F\u002Fv2.tauri.app\u002Fstart\u002Fprerequisites\u002F",[32],"prérequis Tauri",", puis :",[387,388,392],"pre",{"className":389,"code":390,"language":391,"meta":107,"style":107},"language-bash shiki shiki-themes github-light github-dark","bun install\nbun run tauri:serve\n","bash",[342,393,394,406],{"__ignoreMap":107},[395,396,398,402],"span",{"class":397,"line":248},"line",[395,399,401],{"class":400},"sScJk","bun",[395,403,405],{"class":404},"sZZnC"," install\n",[395,407,408,410,413],{"class":397,"line":108},[395,409,401],{"class":400},[395,411,412],{"class":404}," run",[395,414,415],{"class":404}," tauri:serve\n",[14,417,418,355,421,41,424,427,428,77],{},[342,419,420],{},"npm",[342,422,423],{},"pnpm",[342,425,426],{},"deno"," marchent aussi. Build de production : ",[342,429,430],{},"bun run tauri:build",[14,432,433,436,437,442,443,446,447,77],{},[38,434,435],{},"Windows uniquement :"," chaque compile Windows inclut ASIO via le ",[28,438,441],{"href":439,"rel":440},"https:\u002F\u002Fwww.steinberg.net\u002Fasiosdk",[32],"Steinberg ASIO SDK",". Lance ",[342,444,445],{},"bun run setup:asio"," une fois (SDK pas dans git). Linux et macOS utilisent PipeWire \u002F Core Audio — ignore cette étape. Détails : ",[28,448,451],{"href":